The generic camelCase→snake_case covers all these. I'll go with the generic approach plus whitelist.

Actually, wait — should an unrecognized type result in no filtering, or should it map to something? The provider only appends when both column and typeValue are non-null. If type is unrecognized and we pass null column, the query returns everything (with other conditions). That's a reasonable fallback.

